## Type Definitions
- Prefer interfaces over type aliases for object definitions
- Use type aliases for unions and complex types
- Define strict prop interfaces for all components
- Use generics sparingly and with constraints
- Avoid using `any` - use `unknown` instead
- Use `Record<K, T>` instead of `{ [key: string]: T }`

## Naming Conventions
- Prefix interfaces with `I` (e.g., `IUser`)
- Suffix type aliases with `Type` (e.g., `UserType`)
- Use `Props` suffix for component props (e.g., `ButtonProps`)
- Use `Handler` suffix for event handlers (e.g., `clickHandler`)
- Prefix boolean variables with `is`, `has`, or `should`

## Best Practices
- Use mapped types over repetition
- Leverage utility types (Pick, Omit, Partial, Required)
- Define API response types
- Use template literal types for string unions
- Type async functions with Promise return type
- Use branded types for type safety
- Avoid type assertions unless necessary

## Error Handling
- Define custom error types
- Use discriminated unions for error states
- Type error boundaries properly
- Handle null and undefined explicitly
- Use optional chaining and nullish coalescing

